{"Q45949":{"facts":{"period":"គ.ស. ៨៩៣","heritage":[{"km":null,"en":"World Heritage Site"}],"descEn":"Khmer Temple that has territorial conflict between Cambodia and Thailand"},"history":{"en":{"text":"Preah Vihear (lit. \"vihāra of the gods\") (Khmer: ប្រាសាទព្រះវិហារ Prasat Preah Vihear) is an ancient edifice built by the Khmer Empire as a Hindu temple on top of a 525-metre (1,722 ft) cliff in the Dângrêk Mountains, in Cambodia. Over time, it became a Buddhist temple.\nAs a key edifice of the empire's spiritual life, Preah Vihear was supported and modified by successive kings and thus bears elements of several architectural styles.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preah_Vihear"}},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/256992228","wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q45949","village":null},"Q76493583":{"facts":{"descEn":"archaeological site in Preah Vihear Province, Cambodia"},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/13097149349","wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q76493583","village":null},"Q76588552":{"facts":{"descEn":"archaeological site in Preah Vihear Province, Cambodia"},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/13097152703","wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q76588552","village":null},"Q67207152":{"facts":{"descEn":"Archaeological site in Preah Vihear"},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/13101531989","wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q67207152","village":null},"Q67206389":{"facts":{"descEn":"Archaeological site in Preah Vihear"},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/13101604081","wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q67206389","village":null},"Q67201868":{"facts":{"descEn":"Archaeological site in Preah Vihear"},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/13101623262","wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q67201868","village":null},"Q67201897":{"facts":{"descEn":"Archaeological site in Preah Vihear"},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/13299174669","wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q67201897","village":null},"Q67201906":{"facts":{"descEn":"Archaeological site in Preah Vihear"},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/13299180565","wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q67201906","village":null},"Q13016761":{"facts":{},"history":{"km":{"text":"ប្រាសាទដូនតួន មានទីតាំងនៅ បានភូមិសរន ឃុំ សរសរទង់ជ័យ  ស្រុកកន្ធរលក្ស ខេត្តស៊ីសាកេត ។ ចម្ងាយ ៨ គីឡូម៉ែត្រ ពី​ភូមិ ។ ៣៨ គីឡូម៉ែត្រ ពី​ស្រុក​កន្ធរលក្ស ដោយ​ប្រើ​ផ្លូវ​បំបែក​ពី​ផ្លូវជាតិ​លេខ ២២៤៣ គ.ម.៩៨ ចម្ងាយ ៤ គីឡូម៉ែត្រ ជា​ប្រាសាទ​សំខាន់​មួយ​ទៀត។ ស្ថិតនៅជាប់ព្រំដែនប្រទេសថៃ ចំងាយតែ ៣០០ ម៉ែត្រពី ផា ម អ៊ីដែង","url":"https://km.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E1%9E%94%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9E%B6%E1%9E%9F%E1%9E%B6%E1%9E%91%E1%9E%8A%E1%9E%BC%E1%9E%93%E1%9E%8F%E1%9E%BD%E1%9E%93"}},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1418666343","wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13016761","village":null},"Q845513":{"facts":{"period":"សតវត្សទី ១២","heritage":[{"km":null,"en":"Tentative World Heritage Site"}],"descEn":"archaeological site in Preah Vihear Province, Cambodia"},"history":{"km":{"text":"ប្រាសាទព្រះខ័នកំពង់ស្វាយ ត្រូវបានគេស្គាល់ផងដែរថាជា ប្រាសាទបាកាន (យោងទៅតាមការបញ្ចេញសំឡេងក្នុងស្រុក)  មានទីតាំងនៅ ១០០ គីឡូម៉ែត្រ ខាងកើត អង្គរ ក្នុងខេត្តព្រះវិហារ នៃប្រទេសកម្ពុជា។ ​ជា​ប្រាសាទ​សាសនា​ធំ​បំផុត​ដែល​មិន​ធ្លាប់​បាន​សាងសង់​ក្នុង ​សម័យ​អង្គរ ដោយសារ​បរិវេណ​ខាងក្រៅ​មាន​ជាង ២២ គីឡូម៉ែត្រការ៉េ  ទោះបីជាទីតាំងដាច់ស្រយាលធ្វើឱ្យក្លាយជាតំបន់ដែលមិនសូវមានអ្នកទស្សនាក៏ដោយ។","url":"https://km.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%87%E1%9E%81%E1%9F%90%E1%9E%93%E1%9E%80%E1%9F%86%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%84%E1%9F%8B%E1%9E%9F%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9C%E1%9E%B6%E1%9E%99"},"en":{"text":"The archeological complex of Preah Khan Kampong Svay (Khmer: ព្រះខ័ននៅកំពង់ស្វាយ), also known as Prasat Bakan (according to local pronunciation), or Bakan Svay Rolay, is located 100 km east of Angkor, in the Preah Vihear province of Cambodia. It stands as the largest single religious complex ever built during the Angkorian Era, as its exterior enclosure is over 22 km square, even if the isolated location makes it one of the less-visited Angkorian sites.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preah_Khan_Kompong_Svay"}},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/6948899","wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q845513","village":null},"Q1778458":{"facts":{"heritage":[{"km":null,"en":"Tentative World Heritage Site"},{"km":null,"en":"World Heritage Site"}],"descKm":"ប្រាសាទក្នុងខេត្តព្រះវិហារ ប្រទេសកម្ពុជា","descEn":"capital of the Khmer Empire"},"history":{"km":{"text":"ប្រាសាទកោះកេរ្តិ៍ គឺជាទីតាំងបុរាណវត្ថុដែលដាច់ស្រយាលមួយនៅភាគខាងជើង នៅខេត្តព្រះវិហារ នៃប្រទេសកម្ពុជា ដែលមានចម្ងាយប្រហែល ១២០គីឡូម៉ែត្រ ពីខេត្តសៀមរាប និងជារមណីយដ្ឋានអង្គរ។ ជាតំបន់ពោលពេញទៅដោយព្រៃជាច្រើនអនេកដែលមានប្រជាជនរស់នៅតិចតួច។  ជម្រកជាង១៨០ ត្រូវបានរកឃើញនៅក្នុងតំបន់ការពារដែលមានផ្ទៃដី ៨១គីឡូម៉ែត្រការ៉េ ។ តំបន់មិនទាន់ត្រូវបានដោះមីនទាំងស្រុងនោះទេ។","url":"https://km.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E1%9E%94%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9E%B6%E1%9E%9F%E1%9E%B6%E1%9E%91%E1%9E%80%E1%9F%84%E1%9F%87%E1%9E%80%E1%9F%81%E1%9E%9A"},"en":{"text":"Koh Ker (Khmer: ប្រាសាទកោះកេរ្ដិ៍, Prasat Kaôh Kértĕ [praːsaːt kɑh keː]) is a remote archaeological site in northern Cambodia about 120 kilometres (75 mi) away from Siem Reap and the ancient site of Angkor. It is a jungle filled region that is sparsely populated. More than 180 sanctuaries were found in a protected area of 81 square kilometres (31 sq mi). Only about two dozen monuments can be visited by tourists because most of the sanctuaries are hidden in the forest and the whole area is not fully demined.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koh_Ker"}},"osm":null,"wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1778458","village":null},"Q67205947":{"facts":{"descEn":"Archaeological site in Preah Vihear"},"history":{},"osm":null,"wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q67205947","village":null},"Q67201662":{"facts":{"descEn":"archaeological site in Preah Vihear Province, Cambodia"},"history":{},"osm":null,"wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q67201662","village":null},"Q67206475":{"facts":{"descEn":"Archaeological site in Preah Vihear"},"history":{},"osm":null,"wikidata":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q67206475","village":null},"node-148819178":{"facts":{},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/148819178","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-148819180":{"facts":{},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/148819180","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-148819181":{"facts":{},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/148819181","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-1467565207":{"facts":{"period":"សតវត្សទី ៩"},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1467565207","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-2172739895":{"facts":{"period":"សតវត្សទី ១២"},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2172739895","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-2172739896":{"facts":{"period":"សតវត្សទី ១២"},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2172739896","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-2174681659":{"facts":{},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2174681659","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-2174681660":{"facts":{},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2174681660","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-2174681661":{"facts":{},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2174681661","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-2174681662":{"facts":{},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2174681662","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-2174681663":{"facts":{},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2174681663","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-2174681665":{"facts":{},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2174681665","wikidata":null,"village":null},"node-2174681668":{"facts":{},"history":{},"osm":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2174681668","wikidata":null,"village":null},"no